================================================================================
SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE — THIRD-PARTY ARTIFACTS ARE NOT COVERED
================================================================================

The MIT grant above applies ONLY to the code written for this re-implementation:

  * app/                 (local HTTP server and web front end, incl. i18n.js)
  * pr_engine/           (pure-Python re-implementation of the network)
  * pr_cli.py            (command-line entry point)
  * scripts/             (self-check and verification scripts)
  * the English/Chinese documentation in this repository

The following files are THIRD-PARTY artifacts. They are redistributed here
**unmodified**, solely so that the numerical verification documented in the
README can be reproduced. They remain the property of their original authors
(University College Dublin / Shields laboratory and the PeptideRanker authors),
and this MIT license does NOT apply to them:

  * PeptideRanker            (original 2010 Linux x86-64 ELF binary)
  * PeptideRanker.pl         (original Perl wrapper script)
  * Models_Short/            (15 published .model weight files)
  * Models_Long/             (15 published .model weight files)
  * Models_Short.txt         (original model manifest)
  * Models_Long.txt          (original model manifest)
  * testfile.txt             (original example input)
  * README                   (original upstream readme, kept verbatim)

If you intend to reuse those artifacts, obtain permission from the original
authors and respect their terms. Nothing in this repository grants you rights
to them.

Original method and data:
  Mooney C, Haslam NJ, Pollastri G, Shields DC. "Towards the Improved Discovery
  and Design of Functional Peptides: Common Features of Diverse Classes Permit
  Generalized Prediction of Bioactivity." PLoS ONE, 2012.
  Original server: http://distilled.ucd.ie/PeptideRanker/
